.TH rayscan 1  "rayscan 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
rayscan \- An accuracy\-first TCP port scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrayscan\fR [\fB\-\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-db\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
An accuracy\-first TCP/UDP scanner. Rayscan uses a bounded worker pool, adaptive per\-host timeouts, a global rate limit, and a short service\-verification read so a bare handshake from a tarpit or SYN proxy is not reported as an open service. Responsive services are identified from their banners, including common products and versions. On Linux, \-\-syn performs raw SYN discovery and verifies responsive candidates over TCP. A UDP scanner is available for service detection on ports that accept UDP traffic.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<THEME>\fR
Color theme for tables, progress, and diagnostics
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
hacker
.IP \(bu 2
minimal
.IP \(bu 2
cyber
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory for the local NVD advisory database
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rayscan\-scan(1)
Scan TCP ports on one or more targets
.TP
rayscan\-diff(1)
Compare two previous scan reports or state files to display differences
.TP
rayscan\-merge(1)
Merge reports from distributed/sharded scans into one report
.TP
rayscan\-doctor(1)
Check permissions, terminal support, and scan capabilities
.TP
rayscan\-db(1)
Manage the local NVD CVE advisory database
.TP
rayscan\-interactive(1)
Set up and run a scan with guided prompts
.TP
rayscan\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  rayscan scan \-\-target 127.0.0.1 \-\-ports 1\-1024
  rayscan scan \-t 10.0.0.0/24 \-p 22,80,443 \-\-json
  rayscan scan \-t 10.77.0.2 \-p 1\-10000 \-\-profile careful \-\-show all
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
